<title>UK: M&amp;S sets board changes, Sieff to non-exec.</title>
<headline>M&amp;S sets board changes, Sieff to non-exec.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>British retailer Marks &amp; Spencer Plc on Wednesday reported a number of changes to its board of directors, including the retiral of franchise business director Nigel Colne and David Sieff's change of status to non-executive from executive.</p>
<p>Sieff, who comes from one of the company's founding families, will be reappointed as a non-executive director on April 1, 1997, the day after he retires as an executive.</p>
<p>He is currently responsible for corporate and external affairs.</p>
</text>
